---
// MAJO Law system page: Normal Law and Floating Law node reference with in-game node icons, one patch-note style container.
import MajoLayout from '../../../layouts/majo/LandingLayout.astro';
import { LAW_BOARDS, LAW_MATERIALS } from '../../../data/majo/law.js';
import '../../../styles/games/majo/majo-updates.css';
import '../../../styles/games/majo/majo-law.css';

const R2 = 'https://pub-dd9a9c01bc7a43d0bb977b255815a5c4.r2.dev/majo/law';

const normalBoards = LAW_BOARDS.filter((b) => b.law === 'Normal Law');
const floatingBoards = LAW_BOARDS.filter((b) => b.law === 'Floating Law');
---

<MajoLayout
  title="Law System"
  description={`MAJO: Witches Night Law system guide: Normal Law and Floating Law nodes, verification, faction and attack type stat boosts, reject rules and all node effects, updated September 2026.`}
  gameTitle="Law System"
  crumbName="Law System"
>
  <section>
    <article class="majo-update-detail">
      <div class="majo-update-detail-art">
        <img
          src={`${R2}/law-hero.webp`}
          alt="Normal Law and Floating Law star charts in game"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
          width={2000}
          height={1000}
        />
      </div>

      <div class="majo-event-head">
        <span class="majo-update-cat update-cat-news">Progression</span>
        <span class="majo-update-date">Account-wide stat boosts</span>
      </div>

      <h1 class="majo-law-title">
        <img class="majo-law-emblem" src={`${R2}/law-emblem.webp`} alt="" loading="eager" decoding="async" width={308} height={383} />
        Law System
      </h1>

      <p class="majo-law-intro">
        The Law menu, called Fictional Law in game, is the account-wide stat boost system: every
        verified node grants Battle Enhancement effects shared by all Witches. It holds two systems,
        the permanent Normal Law (blue star chart) and the seasonal Floating Law (red star chart),
        and its nodes boost Witches by class, by attack type (Physical, Magic, Mental) and by faction
        (Human, Android, Beastfolk), which is why those two chips now appear on every witch page and
        team build.
      </p>

      <h2 class="majo-event-subtitle">How it works</h2>
      <ul class="majo-update-points">
        <li>Verify nodes to gain their effects. Most nodes have 3 or 5 levels, shown in game as per-level values like 4/8/12/16/20.</li>
        <li>Verify a set number of nodes on a page to unlock the next page. Pages 2 and 3 both unlock through verification counts.</li>
        <li>The first node of a page is a Medium Node: witch teams that meet its condition receive an Overwrite Effect, such as [Class Resonance], immediately on verification.</li>
        <li>Changed your mind? Reject resets a Law's nodes and refunds all upgrade costs, paid in Omen Stones. The number of rejections is limited, and per the official Sep 7 notice a Law Reject reset was added, refreshing weekly on Mondays at 05:00 (UTC+8) from Sept 14, 2026.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="majo-event-subtitle">Verification materials</h2>
      <div class="majo-law-materials">
        {LAW_MATERIALS.map((mt) => (
          <div class="majo-law-material">
            <img class="majo-law-material-icon" src={`${R2}/${mt.icon}.webp`} alt={mt.name} loading="lazy" decoding="async" width={500} height={500} />
            <p class="majo-law-material-name">{mt.name}</p>
            <p class="majo-law-material-law">{mt.law}</p>
            <p class="majo-law-material-note">{mt.note}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <h2 class="majo-event-subtitle">Normal Law (permanent)</h2>
      <ul class="majo-update-points">
        <li>Three pages of 12 nodes each, verified with Normal Law · Inspiration, with Key Law · Conviction as the higher material.</li>
        <li>Core stat nodes boost every Witch: Attack, Defense and Health lines.</li>
        <li>Type nodes boost only Witches of that attack type: Attack (Physical), Attack (Magic), Attack (Mental) and the matching Defense lines.</li>
        <li>Named nodes to watch: Interference Authorization I (all Witches start battles with 120 Extreme Skill Charge), Dislocation Pulse (posture value +30), and Reactive Resonance (Stagger Resistance +2 while casting Extremes, the node the loading tips call the third stage of the Normal Law).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="majo-event-subtitle">Floating Law (seasonal)</h2>
      <ul class="majo-update-points">
        <li>Seasonal boards verified with Floating Law · Echo S1 and Echo S2 materials, currently Season 1.</li>
        <li>Floating Law effects do not apply to battles in the main story chapters, in game notice states this directly.</li>
        <li>Faction nodes boost Witches of one faction: Attack and Defense (Human), (Android) and (Beastfolk) lines on every page, plus Health lines on page 3.</li>
        <li>Faction Resonance nodes add battle-wide perks: bonus Extreme energy at battle start, Critical Resistance, Stagger Resistance and posture, knockdown-triggered Attack buffs and more.</li>
        <li>Each page also carries a unique capstone: Extreme Overclock (page 1), Ascending Sequence (page 2), Stress Pulse (page 3) and Lossless Conduction Trigger on the bonus board.</li>
      </ul>

      {normalBoards.map((b) => (
        <div class="majo-law-board">
          <h3 class="majo-law-board-title">{b.law}, {b.page}</h3>
          <div class="majo-law-rows">
            {b.nodes.map((n) => (
              <div class="majo-law-row">
                <img class="majo-law-node-icon" src={`${R2}/icon-${n.icon}.webp`} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width={72} height={72} />
                <p class="majo-law-node-text"><strong>{n.name}:</strong> {n.desc}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}

      {floatingBoards.map((b) => (
        <div class="majo-law-board">
          <h3 class="majo-law-board-title">{b.law}, {b.page}</h3>
          {b.note && <p class="majo-law-board-note">{b.note}</p>}
          <div class="majo-law-rows">
            {b.nodes.map((n) => (
              <div class="majo-law-row">
                <img class="majo-law-node-icon" src={`${R2}/icon-${n.icon}.webp`} alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width={72} height={72} />
                <p class="majo-law-node-text"><strong>{n.name}:</strong> {n.desc}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}

      <h2 class="majo-event-subtitle">Factions and attack types</h2>
      <ul class="majo-update-points">
        <li>Every Witch has one attack type, Physical, Magic or Mental, and one faction, Human, Android or Beastfolk. Both are shown as chips on witch pages and in team builds.</li>
        <li>Law nodes boost stats by both axes, so a Mental Beastfolk Witch like Jenny feeds on different nodes than a Magic Human like Peseshet.</li>
        <li>Current roster split: 11 Human, 10 Beastfolk and 9 Android Witches.</li>
        <li>Factions also gate content: the Tower of Anomalies has three Faction Recon Zones, Human, Beastfolk and Android, available for a limited time after each version update, with Human-faction Witches required in the Human zone.</li>
      </ul>

      <p class="majo-update-source">
        Sources: in-game Law, StarCharts and tutorial strings from game data (Sep 14, 2026 pull); node icons, board art and material art extracted from the game's UI bundles; official September Update Content Overview (Sep 7, 2026) for the Law Reject reset schedule.
      </p>
    </article>

    <p class="majo-update-back">
      <a href="/guides/majo/">Back to MAJO guides</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</MajoLayout>
